
export anchor Story_0bf15ea7eb7b30c4:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        When a story is drafted, with "Draft with agent" or "Ask agent", accepting
        its suggestions never changes the story that was drafted. Instead, every
        suggestion becomes a new story of its own.

        Once this is done:
        - Accepting what was the story's rewrite, its first piece, adds a new
          story at the end of the Backlog, marked "From agent". The new story has
          the proposed title, prompt, mode, and spec citations, and carries the
          proposed Spec follow-up step as its own step.
        - Each other piece the draft split off is still a new story at the end of
          the Backlog, as now.
        - On a draft about a story, no proposal card reads "Rewrite this story" or
          "Add to this story". Each reads "New story", and the follow-up step shows
          as part of the story it follows, not as a card that adds to the drafted
          story.
        - "Accept all" creates all of them together, in the order given.
        - The drafted story keeps its title, prompt, mode, steps, and citations,
          and stays in its column: a Draft story is no longer moved to the Backlog
          when its draft is accepted.
        - Accepting never marks it "Updated by agent".

        Change spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.drafting,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.draftingWithAgent,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.proposals and
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.proposalCards to say this. Keep where
        new stories go as spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.creating says. Then
        change the code to match.

        Proposals from "Draft stories", from research, and from Ask answers that
        add to a named story are not part of this, and work as they do now.
        \\\

    mode: combined

    model: opus
